     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div> It&#39;s been a busy week. <b>secr</b> 4.3.1 (now on CRAN) has some significant <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/secr%204.3.1%20NEWS.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/secr%25204.3.1%2520NEWS.txt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487107214000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3PCaYIyXsXMVwfWNjBY7aR\">bug fixes and a few new features</a>. The first serious release of <b>secrapp</b> (a Shiny app for running secr) is now <a href=\"https://www.stats.otago.ac.nz/secrapp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.stats.otago.ac.nz/secrapp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487107214000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Efd7r_9riP0f_zNpGbfh1\">live</a> (note also the <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secrapp-tutorial.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secrapp-tutorial.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487107214000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2biCSklfzeIxsNLEVJ01eX\">step-by-step guide</a>). Changes in <b>openCR </b>1.4.2 and 1.4.4 are <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/package=openCR/NEWS\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/package%3DopenCR/NEWS&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487107214000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3kj627z-tXonqsYxEIuron\">minor</a>. The <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487107214000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1dC7gxYKSax_E5ZCIVN04v\">Density web page</a> has been updated: it&#39;s time to push the old Windows application Density into the background. <a href=\"https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/examples/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/examples/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487107214000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1b6q3CBP042TnPyebIH3zG\">Raw input files</a> are provided there for various examples.<br></div><div><br></div><div>The <a href=\"https://www.stats.otago.ac.nz/secrapp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.stats.otago.ac.nz/secrapp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487107214000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Efd7r_9riP0f_zNpGbfh1\">live</a> link lets you run <b>secrapp</b> on a University of Otago machine without installing it yourself. We will see how this works out: peaks in demand may crash it, so for class use etc. you will probably want to run it locally (see <a href=\"https://github.com/MurrayEfford/secrapp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/MurrayEfford/secrapp&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792487107214000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0dN1NPt52mwFzAIHkjH523\">GitHub</a>).<br></div></div>"
